    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0058" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg46"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/2855<hi
                        rendition="#superscript">27/28</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-01T11:00:00+02:00">August 1, 1940—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 1—10:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>777. I am reliably informed that important officials of the German Embassy here
                    have declared on several occasions that Roosevelt’s defeat is of vital
                    importance to Germany; that the German Government has authentic information of
                    an undertaking by the President to bring the United States into the war after
                    the elections and that Germany will therefore spare neither money nor effort to
                    prevent his reelection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
